{title: You and I}
{lyricist: Sergio Rykov}
{composer: Sergio Rykov}

{start_of_verse}
The leaves have not yet fallen,
the grass is still so green
The birds flew up in flocks together,
love left my heart for good
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
Reflections keep on changing
in the still of Moscow ponds
Our gestures slowly melted
and no words are left unsaid
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
Like in a fairy tale, patterns were born,
weaving into mirage
The bonds have shattered to pieces,
and we're no more: you and I
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
We can't bring back what has passed us,
no use to even start
The old quarrels have all faded,
forgotten the seal of hurt
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
Anxiety wandered under the skin,
looking for words to get out
You cannot glue fear to love
and hide it in tears of the soul
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
The heart is looking straight ahead
and believes it will find
And step by step, so stubborn,
another heart comes its way
{end_of_verse}
